.\" Man page for qabas (QabasOne system administration CLI)
.TH QABAS 1 "August 2026" "qabas" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qabas \- QabasOne system administration CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qabas
[\fIglobal-flags\fR]
\fIcommand\fR
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qabas
is the official system administration CLI for QabasOne.
It is the deployment engine: it installs, upgrades, downgrades, backs up,
and operates the QabasOne product stack (API, App, and Dash).
.PP
Product releases are defined in the
.B qabas1-deploy
repository; this CLI does not hardcode a release catalog.
.PP
The Debian package installs only the
.B qabas
binary under
.IR /usr/bin/qabas .
Product configuration and state live under
.I /etc/qabasone
and
.IR /var/lib/qabasone .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the plan without changing the system.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Assume yes for confirmation prompts.
.TP
.B \-\-non\-interactive
Fail instead of prompting for input.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON output.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress human-oriented output.
.TP
.BI \-\-channel " name"
Select the release channel (default: stable).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install [\fIversion\fR]
Install QabasOne (latest stable by default).
.TP
.B uninstall
Uninstall the qabas CLI package. QabasOne services, data, backups, and
configuration are not removed.
.TP
.B deploy \fIversion\fR
Deploy an exact QabasOne product release.
.TP
.B upgrade [\fIversion\fR]
Upgrade to the latest compatible stable release.
.TP
.B downgrade \fIversion\fR
Downgrade to an older release (blocked if unsafe).
.TP
.B rollback
Return to the previous successfully deployed release.
.TP
.B release list|show|current|latest
Inspect published and installed product releases.
.TP
.B backup create|list|verify|show
Create and inspect local backups of persistent state.
.TP
.B restore \fIbackup\-id\fR
Restore QabasOne from a backup.
.TP
.B status
Show installed release and service health.
.TP
.B ps
List QabasOne containers.
.TP
.B up [\fIservice\fR] [\fB-d\fR] [\fB--build\fR]
Start all services, or one service. The \fB-d\fR flag keeps containers detached, and \fB--build\fR builds images before starting.
.TP
.B start [\fIservice\fR]
Start all services, or one service.
.TP
.B down [\fIservice\fR]
Stop and remove all QabasOne service containers, or one service container, while preserving data.
.TP
.B stop [\fIservice\fR]
Stop all services, or one service.
.TP
.B restart [\fIservice\fR]
Restart all services, or one service.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose host, Docker, and installation health (includes logs UI status,
memory, disk, Docker disk usage, and autopilot).
.TP
.B guide [\fItopic\fR] [\fB--name\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB--host\fR \fIip\fR] [\fB--writer\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB--no-detect\fR]
Print step-by-step walkthroughs (install, replica, backup, schedule, pitr, dr,
maintenance). Each step says where to run it and shows commands pre-filled from
read-only detection of this machine (role, address, SSH host key, cluster
nodes), marked done, todo, or blocked. Without a topic, prints the detected
machine summary, suggested next topics, and the topic list.
.TP
.B logs [\fIservice\fR]
Show service logs via Docker Compose.
.TP
.B logs ui up|down|status|open
Start or stop a localhost realtime logs web UI (Dozzle). Optional
.B --full
adds Loki, Alloy, and Grafana for searchable history. Runs as Compose project
.B qabas1-logs
(separate from the product stack). Binds to 127.0.0.1 only with auth enabled
by default; passwords live in
.I /etc/qabasone/logs-ui.credentials
\&. Full-stack containers define healthchecks;
.B up --full
waits until healthy. Loki is not published on the host. Dozzle and Alloy reach
Docker only through a read-only socket proxy on an internal network; every
logs UI container drops all capabilities and runs read-only. Alloy masks
secrets before lines reach Loki, which keeps
.B QABAS_LOGS_RETENTION
(default 7d).
.TP
.B logs retention [\fB--apply\fR]
Show how each log is bounded (qabas.log, history, container logs, Loki) and
its current size.
.B --apply
rotates over-cap files now.
.TP
.B auth status|set|get|unset|login|logout
Manage GitHub (private repos) and GHCR (container pull) credentials.
Both are required before
.B install
/
.BR deploy .
.TP
.B config show|get|set|validate
Show or change local QabasOne configuration.
.TP
.B db migrate|seed
Run database migrations or seed data through the installed Docker Compose project.
.TP
.B auth login|status|logout
Save or inspect GitHub credentials for private QabasOne repos.
.TP
.B maintenance on|off|status
Control maintenance mode. When enabled, the app and dashboard hosts serve a
static maintenance page through
.BR edge-nginx .
The CLI discovers the edge layout from the environment or container mounts and
only toggles files under
.I html/
and
.IR includes/ ;
it never rewrites operator-owned
.B .conf
files. Edge server blocks must already
.B include /etc/nginx/includes/qabas1-maintenance.conf .
Use
.B \-\-for
or
.B \-\-until
to show an expected return time.
Use
.B \-\-page
or
.B QABAS_MAINTENANCE_PAGE
to supply a custom HTML template (supports
.BR {{.Until}} );
.B \-\-page
overrides the environment variable.
.TP
.B autopilot run|enable|disable|status
Unattended hourly self-maintenance, scheduled by
.B install
(opt out with
.BR \-\-no\-autopilot ).
Prunes dangling Docker images and old build cache, removes PITR WAL older
than the oldest kept base backup, applies scheduled-backup retention early
when disk is low (emergency minimum when critical), enables container log
rotation, ends expired maintenance windows, and restarts unhealthy services
(at most 3 times per service per day). Also rotates qabas.log and history
and re-tightens permissions on config, secrets, backups, and logs. Never
deletes volumes or non-scheduled backups. Runs from
.B qabas-autopilot.timer
on Linux and the Task Scheduler task
.B QabasOne\eAutopilot
on Windows.
.TP
.B secrets status
Show each credential's age, file mode, and purpose; flags secrets older than
180 days.
.TP
.B secrets rotate \fIname\fR|all... [\fB--force\fR] [\fB--no-backup\fR]
Rotate postgres, redis, minio, jwt, 2fa, pepper, or logs-ui credentials. Takes
a pre-rotate backup, enables maintenance, updates the database password and
env files atomically, recreates services, and verifies health; on failure
everything is rolled back.
.B all
covers the non-destructive set; 2fa and pepper need
.BR --force .
Writer only.
.TP
.B limits show|sync
Show or regenerate
.IR compose.qabas-limits.yaml :
RAM-sized memory limits, pids limits, no-new-privileges, and dropped
capabilities for each long-running service. Settings from the release compose
are never overridden. Synced on every deploy.
.TP
.B history [\fB--all\fR]
Show deployment and restore audit history.
.B --all
includes rotated archives.
.TP
.B sysinfo [\fB--watch\fR[=\fIinterval\fR]]
Show machine resources: OS, kernel, uptime, CPU model, cores and load, memory
and swap, free disk on the volumes holding QabasOne data, network addresses,
and Docker usage, each graded ok, warn, or crit. Aliases:
.BR machine ,
.BR hostinfo .
.TP
.B version
Print CLI and installed product versions.
.TP
.B update
Update the qabas CLI from GitHub Releases.
.PP
Service lifecycle commands use the Docker Compose project
.B qabasone
and do not manage external reverse proxy containers such as
.BR edge-nginx .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/qabasone/
Configuration, secrets, and compose environment files.
.TP
.I /etc/qabasone/github-token
Saved GitHub PAT for private repo access (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /etc/qabasone/ghcr-token
Saved GHCR PAT for
.B docker login ghcr.io
(mode 0600).
.TP
.I /etc/qabasone/ghcr-username
GitHub username used with the GHCR token.
.TP
.I /var/lib/qabasone/
State, deployments, releases, backups, compose files, and lock file.
.TP
.I /etc/qabasone/secrets.meta.json
Creation and rotation times of each secret (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /var/log/qabasone/qabas.log
One redacted line per command; rotated at 10 MiB, 5 gzip archives kept.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
.TQ
.B GH_TOKEN
GitHub PAT for private repos (overrides saved github token).
.TP
.B GHCR_TOKEN
.TQ
.B QABAS_GHCR_TOKEN
PAT for
.B ghcr.io
pulls (overrides saved ghcr token; needs
.BR read:packages ).
.TP
.B GHCR_USERNAME
Docker login username for
.B ghcr.io
(overrides saved username).
.TP
.B QABAS_CONFIG_DIR
Override the configuration directory (default:
.IR /etc/qabasone ).
.TP
.B QABAS_STATE_DIR
Override the state directory (default:
.IR /var/lib/qabasone ).
.TP
.B QABAS_LOG_DIR
Override the log directory (default:
.IR /var/log/qabasone ).
.TP
.B QABAS_LOCK_PATH
Override the lock file path.
.TP
.B QABAS_DEPLOY_REPO
Override the deploy definitions repository.
.TP
.B QABAS_DEPLOY_REF
Override the deploy definitions git ref.
.TP
.B QABAS_EDGE_NGINX_DIR
Host nginx root containing
.IR html/ ,
.IR includes/ ,
and
.I conf.d/
(overrides docker mount discovery).
.TP
.B QABAS_EDGE_NGINX_CONTAINER
Edge nginx container name used for mount discovery and reload (default:
.BR edge-nginx ).
.TP
.B QABAS_EDGE_NGINX_CONF
Optional conf file or directory used only to verify that the maintenance
include already exists. Never written by the CLI.
.TP
.B QABAS_MAINTENANCE_PAGE
HTML template for the maintenance page. Overridden by
.BR \-\-page .
Supports
.B {{.Until}}
for the expected return time.
.TP
.B QABAS_LOGS_RETENTION
Loki retention for the logs UI (e.g. 14d, 72h, 2w; default 7d).
.TP
.B QABAS_SOCKET_PROXY_IMAGE
Image for the logs UI Docker socket proxy.
.TP
.B QABAS_LIMITS
Set to
.B off
to stop generating the resource limits overlay.
.TP
.BI QABAS_LIMIT_ SERVICE
Memory limit for one service (e.g.
.BR QABAS_LIMIT_API=2g ;
.B none
removes it).
.SH AUTH
Install and deploy need GitHub (private repos) and GHCR (image pulls).
One PAT with
.B repo
+
.B read:packages
is enough:
.PP
.nf
.RS
export GITHUB_TOKEN="$(gh auth token)"
sudo \-E qabas auth login
sudo qabas auth status
sudo qabas install
.RE
.fi
.PP
If
.I ghcr\-token
is unset,
.B qabas
falls back to the GitHub token.
Before image pull it runs
.B docker login ghcr.io
using the resolved username and token.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid input or configuration.
.TP
.B 3
Compatibility failure.
.TP
.B 4
Health-check failure.
.TP
.B 5
Backup or restore failure.
.TP
.B 6
Network or registry failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install the latest stable product release:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo qabas install
.RE
.fi
.PP
Deploy an exact product version:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo qabas deploy 2.8.0
.RE
.fi
.PP
Save credentials for subsequent sudo invocations:
.PP
.nf
.RS
export GITHUB_TOKEN="$(gh auth token)"
sudo \-E qabas auth login
.RE
.fi
